Put one timer_list, one work_struct, and one borrowed rk_state pointer in
execution/scheduler.c. Initialize both callback objects before the first
mod_timer().

The timer callback should only increment timer_fires, call schedule_work(), and
rearm itself. The work callback reads actions_enabled once and increments
actions_completed when it is true.

On unload, remove procfs first. Then use timer_shutdown_sync() before
cancel_work_sync(), and destroy state only after both calls return.
